# Helm API — local environment
#
# Bun reads apps/api/.env (generated). Do not hand-edit .env.
#
# Setup with 1Password CLI (recommended):
#   1. op signin
#   2. Copy the block for the Product you want into a file of the same name
#      (see "Product input files" below). Set your absolute paths.
#   3. pnpm sync-env -- <product>     # leasity-tenants | helm
#   4. pnpm dev
#
# Secret values live in 1Password. In the product files use references:
#   op://Vault/item/field
# Never paste raw tokens into the product files.
#
# Without 1Password: copy a product block into .env and replace op://… with
# real values (not recommended).
#
# ─── Variables ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# HELM_KNOWLEDGE_REPO_PATH  Absolute path to the Product knowledge repo
#                           (directory that contains .helm/product.yaml).
# HELM_DATA_DIR             Absolute path to Helm operational data/.
# GITHUB_TOKEN              GitHub PAT (Projects + repo API).
#                           1Password: op://Helm/helm/github-token
# GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET     Shared secret for GitHub → Helm webhooks.
# LINEAR_API_KEY            Linear PAT — only when Product uses Linear
#                           (Arriendo Fácil). Helm-the-product uses GitHub
#                           Projects and does not need this key.
#
# ─── Product input files (gitignored; used by sync-env) ──────────────────────
#
# Create apps/api/.env.leasity-tenants  OR  apps/api/.env.helm
# Then:  pnpm sync-env -- leasity-tenants   |   pnpm sync-env -- helm
#
# --- .env.leasity-tenants (Arriendo Fácil / Linear) ---
# HELM_KNOWLEDGE_REPO_PATH=/Users/you/Git/Leasity/leasity-tenants-knowledge
# HELM_DATA_DIR=/Users/you/Git/Leasity/helm-data
# GITHUB_TOKEN=op://Helm/helm/github-token
# LINEAR_API_KEY=op://Leasity/leasity-tenants/linear-api-key
# GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=op://Leasity/leasity-tenants/github-webhook-secret
# LINEAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET=op://Leasity/leasity-tenants/linear-webhook-secret
#
# --- .env.helm (Helm self-dogfood / GitHub Projects) ---
# HELM_KNOWLEDGE_REPO_PATH=/Users/you/Git/Helm/helm-knowledge
# HELM_DATA_DIR=/Users/you/Git/Helm/helm/apps/api/data
# GITHUB_TOKEN=op://Helm/helm/github-token
# GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=op://Helm/helm/github-webhook-secret
